{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"files\":[{\"content\":\"#include<stdio.h>\\n#include<stdlib.h>\\n#include<string.h>\\n\\n/* Maximum size (in char) for neighbors and compute lists */\\n#define MAX 100\\n\\ntypedef struct {\\n  int id;\\n  float value;\\n  char neighbors[MAX];\\n} Node;\\n\\ntypedef struct {\\n  float value;\\n  unsigned char ready;\\n} CostEntry;\\n\\n/* Reads input, allocates memory, writes graph size and node list. Returns the graph. */\\nNode* read_input(char* fname, int *n, char* list) {\\n  Node* data = NULL;\\n  FILE *fl = NULL;\\n\\n  if (fname == NULL)\\n    fl = stdin;\\n  else\\n    fl = fopen(fname, \\\"r\\\");\\n\\n  if (fl == NULL) {\\n    fprintf(stderr, \\\"Error!\\\\n\\\");\\n    exit(1);\\n  }\\n\\n  // header\\n  fscanf(fl, \\\"%d %[^\\n]\\\", n, list);\\n\\n  if (*n > 0) {\\n    data = (Node*) malloc ((*n)*sizeof(Node));\\n    if(data == NULL){\\n      fprintf(stderr, \\\"Error!\\\\n\\\");\\n      exit(1);\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  for(int i = 0; i < *n; i++)\\n    fscanf(fl, \\\"%d %f %[^\\n]\\\", &data[i].id, &data[i].value, data[i].neighbors);\\n\\n  fclose(fl);\\n  return data;\\n}\\n\\n/* Returns the index of the node with the given id or -1 if not found */\\nint find_by_id(Node g[], int id, int size){\\n  int i = 0;\\n\\n  while((i < size) && g[i].id != id)\\n    i++;\\n\\n  if(i < size)\\n    return i;\\n\\n  return -1;\\n}\\n\\n/* Computes and caches the sum for the node with the given id */\\nfloat get_costly(Node *g, int id, int size, CostEntry *cache) {\\n  int nd = find_by_id(g, id, size);\\n  if(nd < 0)\\n    return 0;\\n\\n  if(cache[nd].ready)\\n    return cache[nd].value;\\n\\n  int idmax = -1;\\n  float max = 0;\\n  char aux[MAX];\\n  char *auxptr;\\n  strcpy(aux, g[nd].neighbors);\\n  char *t = strtok_r(aux, \\\" \\\", &auxptr);\\n\\n  while(t != NULL) {\\n    int neighbor_id = atoi(t);\\n    int d = find_by_id(g, neighbor_id, size);\\n    if (d >= 0 && max < g[d].value) {\\n      max = g[d].value;\\n      idmax = neighbor_id;\\n    }\\n    t = strtok_r(NULL, \\\" \\\", &auxptr);\\n  }\\n\\n  float r = g[nd].value;\\n  if(idmax != -1)\\n    r += get_costly(g, idmax, size, cache);\\n\\n  cache[nd].value = r;\\n  cache[nd].ready = 1;\\n  return r;\\n}\\n\\n/* Main program - calls read input, computes sum for each node in the list, prints output */\\nint main() {\\n  char *fileN = NULL;\\n  char computelist[MAX];\\n  int n = -1;\\n  Node* input = NULL;\\n\\n  input = read_input(fileN, &n, computelist);\\n\\n  CostEntry *cache = (CostEntry*) calloc(n > 0 ? n : 1, sizeof(CostEntry));\\n  if(cache == NULL) {\\n    fprintf(stderr, \\\"Error!\\\\n\\\");\\n    free(input);\\n    exit(1);\\n  }\\n\\n  // process\\n  for(char *c = strtok(computelist, \\\" \\\"); c != NULL; c = strtok(NULL, \\\" \\\"))\\n    printf(\\\"%s: %f\\\\n\\\", c, get_costly(input, atoi(c), n, cache));\\n\\n  free(cache);\\n  free(input);\\n  return 0;\\n}\\n\",\"path\":\"src/graph.c\"}],\"hypothesis\":\"On a DAG, requested start nodes can share downstream paths. Caching each computed result by the node's array index should avoid revisiting those paths and reparsing their neighbor lists; a dense cache also keeps result lookups compact. Reusing a cached float preserves the recursive result already returned for that node.\",\"notes\":\"The cache is populated only after a node's recursive result is computed, retaining the original neighbor selection order and accumulation order. No benchmark-input specialization is used.\",\"research\":{\"queries\":[],\"urls\":[]},\"sources_kept\":[],\"transformations\":[\"Added a per-node-index result cache shared across requested start-node computations.\",\"Allocated cache entries contiguously and initialized them to an uncomputed state with calloc.\",\"Allocated the node array for any positive graph size, including a single-node graph.\"]}"}}
